1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,580
Start in the folder containing the three ZIP files.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,180
Extract the source code into the current folder.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,380
Extract data/ and cache/ into toy/.
Keep the scripts from the code archive.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,080
Extract the NT-V3 weights into assets/NTv3_8M_pre/.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,380
Enter the extracted project folder.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,680
Check for the model weights. The expected answer is True.

7
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:32,880
This image is already installed. For a first build, run:
docker build -t duetscreen-release:1.0 .

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,700
Run the toy script. It trains for one epoch,
then tests the checkpoint from this run.

9
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:50,900
Epoch 1 of 1 is running. The progress bar counts eight batches.

10
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:04,900
The first batch can take longer while the GPU kernels initialize.

11
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:30,900
This toy run uses just eight training updates.
It demonstrates the training and prediction workflow.

12
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:03,780
Training writes the selected checkpoint to toy/out/seed42_toy/.

13
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:10,300
The script starts a separate prediction container
using the checkpoint just saved.

14
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:21,900
The held-out toy test set contains 20 positives and 20 negatives.

15
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:37,000
At 0.5, all 40 predictions are positive: accuracy is 50%.
Test AUROC is 0.4425 after this single toy epoch.

16
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:41,280
List the saved checkpoints. Prediction used the best_ file.

17
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:46,180
Read the predictions CSV from toy/out/test_pred/.

18
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:52,780
Inspect four test records alongside their predicted labels.

19
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:58,900
All 40 test records have predictions.
The paper reports performance on the full benchmark.
